 "title": "Matt Damon's Biggest Mistake",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "Matt Damon shares a story about turning down 10% of the movie Avatar because he was shooting The Bourne Ultimatum. The creator claims sharing mistakes with confidence and humor makes someone more charismatic and likeable.",
 "key_points": [
  "Matt Damon turned down 10% of Avatar offered by Jim Cameron because he was shooting The Bourne Ultimatum.",
  "Jim Cameron told Damon the movie didn't need a movie star and he would find someone new if Damon didn't do it.",
  "Damon stated he turned it down for moral reasons because he could not walk away from the thing he had spent years doing.",
  "The creator claims the recipe for being charismatic is having the confidence to admit when you messed up, being a fantastic storyteller, and being a person of your work."
 ],
 "content": "Study how Matt Damon shares about his biggest mistake... Matt Damon is clearly one of the most charismatic people in the world. This video showcases one of his tricks. Watch until the end. Clip: @valkyreusclips. I turned down and I will go down in history as the person because Jim Cameron called me, he offered me 10% of Avatar. You will never meet an actor who turned down more money than me, but I was in the middle of shooting The Bourne Ultimatum, and I needed to be around, I needed to be available to do more work in our post-production. He was really lovely and he said, you know, he goes, I if you don't do this, this movie doesn't need you, it doesn't need a movie star at all. He goes, the movie is the star, the idea is the star and and uh and it's going to work. And he goes, so if you don't do it, I'm going to discover some new guy and and put him in. But if you do it, I'll give you 10% of the movie. And for moral reasons, again, I told him I couldn't walk away from this thing that I'd spent all these years doing. He turned down getting a percentage of one of the biggest movies of all time. Most people would be too embarrassed to share something like that. That's probably on his list of the top mistakes he's made. However, he shared that he needed to stay true to his word and have integrity with himself and what he committed to. The ultimate recipe for being charismatic and likeable is having the confidence to say when you've messed up, being a fantastic storyteller, and being a person of your work. What do you think? Did the story make you like him more or think he's an idiot for passing up that deal? Follow for more to learn to communicate like the top 1%. Text on screen: Study how Matt Damon shares about his biggest mistake... Matt Damon's Biggest Mistake. Matt Damon has a natural charisma that makes people instantly like him and want to listen when he speaks. But there’s something very specific he does in this clip that makes him so magnetic, and once you notice it, you’ll start seeing it everywhere. Watch until the end to learn how you can use it to become more charismatic too 🎤 Clip: @valkyreusclips",
